    "summary": "Brooch of overlay technique depicting female flute player Kokopolmana (mana= girl in Hopi) against background of adobe houses. The background is oxidized and scored to produce the relief effect. The design is contemporary and ceremonial events. She is portrayed as rather lascivious a role she enacts in Night Dances in March/April in Hopi villages. The Brooch has a sterling pin with a safety catch. The piece is signed, the makers mark seems to be a tablita.",
